{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "system",
      "content": "Answer in one or two sentences."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "What are server-sent events?"
    }
  ],
  "temperature": 0.7
}

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "stream": true,
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Name three HTTP status codes worth retrying."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "What is the weather in Oslo right now?"
    }
  ],
  "tools": [
    {
      "type": "function",
      "function": {
        "name": "get_weather",
        "description": "Current weather for a city.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "city": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "City name, for example Oslo."
            },
            "unit": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "celsius",
                "fahrenheit"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "city"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "tool_choice": "auto"
}

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "What is the weather in Oslo right now?"
    },
    {{toolTurnAssistant}},
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "{{toolCallId}}",
      "content": "{\"city\":\"Oslo\",\"temperature_c\":4,\"conditions\":\"light rain\"}"
    }
  ],
  "tools": [
    {
      "type": "function",
      "function": {
        "name": "get_weather",
        "description": "Current weather for a city.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "city": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "City name, for example Oslo."
            },
            "unit": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "celsius",
                "fahrenheit"
              ]
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "city"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

{
  "model": "{{model}}",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "What color is the square in this image? Answer with one word."
        },
        {
          "type": "image_url",
          "image_url": {
            "url": "data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAEAAAABACAIAAAAlC+aJAAAAWElEQVR42u3ZQQ0AMAgEQZTgXxReWhUl0MxlDcz74ixfAAAAAAAAAAAAAAC0ASrzaQAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA8wAeGgAAAAAAAAAAAIBvABeLjT5ZV50bxgAAAABJRU5ErkJggg=="
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

item.description:
How failures look on the wire. Check the HTTP status first, then the body, which comes in three shapes:

- A, gateway: `{"error": {"type": "...", "message": "...", ...}}` for 402, 413, 429 quota, 502, 503, 504, and errors inside a stream;
- B, validation: `{"message": "...", "errors": {"field": ["..."]}}` for 422;
- C, bare message: `{"message": "..."}` for 401, the rate-limit 429, and 403 (with `"code": "email_unverified"`).

Some bodies are not JSON at all: Cloudflare's 524 page is HTML. Messages are written for people and can change, so branch on the status, `type`, `code`, `resets_at` and the headers.

Retry 502, 503 `server_busy`, 504, 524 and connection errors with exponential backoff and jitter. On the rate-limit 429, wait `Retry-After`. Never retry quota 429s before `resets_at`, and never retry 401, 402, 403, 413 or 422. The full tables: https://github.com/Moloch-AI/uncensored-ai-api/blob/main/docs/errors.md
